<section class="fragment-benchmark" data-artifact="benchmark" data-slice="lone-forward" data-mode="baseline">
  <!-- @include-skip the metric table is hand-inlined as in the prior revisions of this artifact -->
  <table class="bm-metrics">
    <thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>Baseline (a447ff1)</th><th>Tripwire</th><th>Unit</th><th>Direction</th><th>Role</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr data-role="gate"><td>bench.cpu_us_per_tick</td><td>1.5422</td><td>1.6964</td><td>us</td><td>lower is better</td><td>gate</td></tr>
      <tr data-role="gate"><td>bench.peak_mem_mb</td><td>6.660</td><td>8.33</td><td>MB</td><td>lower is better</td><td>gate</td></tr>
      <tr data-role="report"><td>bench.cpu_ms_per_match</td><td>450.0</td><td>reported (495.0)</td><td>ms</td><td>lower is better</td><td>reported</td></tr>
      <tr data-role="report"><td>bench.match_wall_ms</td><td>449</td><td>budget 2000</td><td>ms</td><td>lower is better</td><td>reported</td></tr>
      <tr data-role="report"><td>bench.ticks_per_match</td><td>291800</td><td>at most 360000</td><td>ticks</td><td>lower is better</td><td>reported</td></tr>
      <tr data-role="report"><td>engine.ticks_per_s</td><td>649889</td><td>none</td><td>ticks/s</td><td>higher is better</td><td>reported</td></tr>
      <tr data-role="report"><td>criterion.tick_step_us</td><td>1.5408</td><td>none</td><td>us</td><td>lower is better</td><td>reported</td></tr>
      <tr data-role="report"><td>criterion.steering_pass_22_ns</td><td>869.58</td><td>none</td><td>ns</td><td>lower is better</td><td>reported</td></tr>
      <tr data-role="report"><td>bench.stream_ticks_per_s</td><td>446862</td><td>none</td><td>ticks/s</td><td>higher is better</td><td>reported</td></tr>
      <tr data-role="gate"><td>bench.stream_peak_mem_mb</td><td>8.207</td><td>10.26</td><td>MB</td><td>lower is better</td><td>stream gate</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <aside class="callout callout-info"><div class="callout-hd">The gate is per tick</div><div class="callout-body">The slice changes the carrier's option scores and the tackle draw, which run on every tick with the ball in play. The slice names no tripwire, so the default rule applies: +10 percent processor time per tick and +25 percent peak memory. Processor time per match is reported beside it; new decision weights and tackle odds change play, so match length may move.</div></aside>

  <aside class="callout callout-info"><div class="callout-hd">A higher per-tick baseline</div><div class="callout-body">1.5422 us per tick is 4.5 percent above the previous baseline (1.4753 us). The defending mechanisms that landed in between explain it, and that slice's gate passed. It is a new baseline, not a regression of this slice.</div></aside>

  <style>
    .fragment-benchmark .bm-metrics { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.9rem; }
    .fragment-benchmark .bm-metrics th, .fragment-benchmark .bm-metrics td { text-align: left; padding: 6px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(127,127,127,0.25); }
    .fragment-benchmark .bm-metrics tr[data-role="gate"] td:first-child { font-weight: 600; }
    .fragment-benchmark .callout { margin-top: 12px; }
  </style>
  <script>
    (function () {
      var root = document.currentScript.closest('.fragment-benchmark');
      var metrics = root ? root.querySelectorAll('.bm-metrics tbody tr').length : 0;
      window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('sdlc:fragment-ready', { detail: { name: 'benchmark', artifact: 'benchmark', counts: { metrics: metrics, regressions: 0, improvements: 0 } } }));
    })();
  </script>
</section>
